lowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"IMO the close brace skipping should only happen after a close brace was automatically added, as it is intended to prevent you from adding an extra close brace in that case. We can keep some temporary state to track this. This way we don't need to know if it is actually balanced. If someone goes back to already written code and they add a brace end, then they probably want it intentionally. I also think VSCode does similar.\r\nI'm thinking it could be a stack of symbols per caret that get added to if the user adds multiple completion pairs, and removed when the close part is added or the caret moves past it. It would clear if the caret goes before the first start pair or after the last end pair.\r\nThe same should be done with backspacing to remove the end brace too.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107091#pullrequestreview-2894530187","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107091","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107091#pullrequestreview-2894530187"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107091"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-04T01:35:14Z","commit_id":"95eccd16ce58ce111b5d361d31ae8d8a3db0ee6d"}]